From dbc98f239dd7be405f7ef009137500c520e110da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:40:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] arm64: rhodep_defconfig: panic and reboot on lockups

As on negroni: a kernel that hangs only comes back if it panics or the
watchdog bites. Turn the soft and hard lockup detectors on with panic,
the hard one in buddy mode, and panic on oops with a 10 s reboot, so a
wedged trial kernel reboots into the loader, which then charges it a
try. test_lockup is there to drill each of them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/rhodep_defconfig | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/rhodep_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/rhodep_defconfig
index 54806fc54..5af3e701e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/rhodep_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/rhodep_defconfig
@@ -1203,3 +1203,10 @@ CONFIG_CORESIGHT_STM=m
 CONFIG_CORESIGHT_CPU_DEBUG=m
 CONFIG_CORESIGHT_CTI=m
 CONFIG_MEMTEST=y
+CONFIG_PANIC_ON_OOPS=y
+CONFIG_PANIC_TIMEOUT=10
+CONFIG_SOFTLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
+CONFIG_BOOTPARAM_SOFTLOCKUP_PANIC=1
+CONFIG_HARDLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
+CONFIG_BOOTPARAM_HARDLOCKUP_PANIC=y
+CONFIG_TEST_LOCKUP=m
